KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--unwindset 'fill<signed_int,3>(ptr_signed_int).0:1' --unwinding-assertions
^\[fill\.unwind\.0\] line \d+ unwinding assertion loop 0: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
--unwindset splits its argument at every comma
(cmdline.get_comma_separated_values), so this entry becomes
`fill<signed_int' and `3>(ptr_signed_int).0:1'; neither matches a loop, and
the bound 1 is silently not applied: the loop is unwound completely and its
unwinding assertion holds.
